      "amount": "1/4 teaspoon"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large comal over medium heat.",
    "Add the chopped onion and cook until it is lightly browned, stirring occasionally.",
    "Add the minced garlic and grated ginger and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the lamb cubes and cook until they are browned on all sides, stirring occasionally.",
    "Add the curry powder and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the raisins, canned diced tomatoes, low-sodium chicken broth, salt, and black pepper, and stir to combine.",
    "Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, for 1.5 hours, or until the lamb is tender.",
    "Serve the curry hot, garnished with chopped fresh cilantro, if desired."
  ],
